{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794539499176,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1dfed7ffelzC6M9OLNWqvFE","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2e3abd4002LuThxAp1568ubY","sessionID":"ses_e2d1dfed7ffelzC6M9OLNWqvFE","messageID":"msg_1d2e39df4001g1AvmGSj5ZN5rk","type":"tool","id":"call_ecae707cc0184733980961d7","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/REPO RULES.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/REPO RULES.md, lines 1-108\n1: # REPO RULES\n2: \n3: Repo-local operating rules. `AGENTS.md` **Gate 5 (§2)** makes reading this mandatory\n4: before your first write of the session; this document then routes you to every rule\n5: file that governs what you are about to do. **It is a router, not a rulebook:** it\n6: holds no rules of its own.\n7: \n8: ---\n9: \n10: ## 1. HOW TO USE THIS\n11: \n12: 1. **Match on the action you are about to take**, not the topic of the request.\n13: 2. **Load before the action.** A rule read afterwards is a post-mortem.\n14: 3. **A file already in context is not re-read.**\n15: 4. **Every trigger that fires is loaded, not just the first.** They compose; the more\n16:    specific wins on conflict. Three and four firing at once is the normal case, not an\n17:    edge case.\n18: 5. **Nothing fires → `AGENTS.md` alone governs.** Do not hunt for a rule to apply.\n19: \n20: ### Precedence\n21: \n22: | Level | Source | Can be overridden? |\n23: |-------|--------|--------------------|\n24: | 1 | Every `AGENTS.md` §1 hard blocker, the Four Laws, PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK, Comment Hygiene, and every mandatory gate in §2 | No |\n25: | 2 | An explicit, in-the-moment operator instruction | Not applicable, it is the instruction |\n26: | 3 | These rule files, and the guidance in a skill's `SKILL.md` | Only by level 1 or 2 |\n27: | 4 | General judgment | By anything above |\n28: \n29: A rule file may tighten `AGENTS.md`. None relaxes a HARD BLOCK or authorizes what\n30: `AGENTS.md` forbids. Gate 5 does not change that: it makes the **load** mandatory,\n31: while what you load stays at level 3, the obligation to read is tier 1, the content\n32: is not.\n33: \n34: ---\n35: \n36: ## 2. TRIGGER TABLE\n37: \n38: | You are about to… | Load | It settles |\n39: |-------------------|------|-----------|\n40: | Add a file, module, class, interface, option, layer, or dependency · write a spec or plan that adds one · generalize something that works · write \"flexible\", \"future-proof\", \"scalable\", \"extensible\", \"might need\", \"best practice\", \"while we're here\" · add a test beyond the coverage floor | [`prevent-overengineering.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md) | Whether this should exist at all, and at what size |\n41: | Touch a file outside the ask · fix something noticed in passing · change something else because it would make the fix easier · rename, reformat, or delete beyond the named area · deviate from an approved plan · decide what to do with the rest when part of the work is blocked · notice a defect, smell or stale comment outside the files in scope | [`scope-discipline.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md) | What is yours to change, and how to raise what isn't |\n42: | Say \"done\", \"works\", \"fixed\", \"passing\", \"no regressions\" · report a result · quote a number · act on a tool's or sub-agent's success report · close out a turn · report a file path or command output · write a completion summary or tick something off as done | [`evidence-and-proof.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md) | What counts as proof, how a green run lies, what an honest close-out contains |\n43: | Decide whether to hand work to another runtime at all · hand it to a CLI executor, sub-agent, fan-out lineage, or deep loop · compose the prompt one will act on · accept or quote what one returned · answer a judgment question from your own reading alone | [`delegation-and-orchestration.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/delegation-and-orchestration.md) | The orchestrating posture, what a brief must carry, why one model is one opinion |\n44: | Delete, overwrite, migrate, deploy, publish, send, install · force-push or rewrite history · change a shared contract · touch auth, data, or config · make any call that leaves this machine · truncate · touch branches, tags, or reflogs | [`blast-radius.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/blast-radius.md) | Reversibility, the rollback sentence, when to stop for a yes |\n45: | Diagnose a failure · make a red check green · attempt the same fix twice · add a special case, retry, sleep, or broadened catch · call a failure a flake, infra, or pre-existing | [`root-cause-and-debugging.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/root-cause-and-debugging.md) | Fixing the producer instead of the symptom, and when to level up to the seam |\n46: | Answer without certainty · contradict the operator · fill a gap with a plausible guess · hit a contradiction between two things that must both be true · name a path, flag, function, version, or number you have not verified · not know while a plausible answer is available · see sources disagree, or the code contradict the spec, the docs or the operator · the operator asserts something you believe is wrong · change a checked answer after pushback or doubt, or drop an approach before it concludes · cite a rule, restriction, policy, limit or permission, or decline a request | [`uncertainty-and-honesty.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/uncertainty-and-honesty.md) | Confidence bands, UNKNOWN, contradiction halts |\n47: | Write any substantive reply, an answer, an explanation, a close-out or a status · draft or edit any sentence a reader will read · present a recommendation, a fork, or a trade-off · start a multi-step stretch of work the reader will not see inside · report what a long autonomous run found · the reader says they did not follow or asks for a plainer version | [`communication.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md) | How a reply reads: answer first, one recommended path, length, filler, plain sentences, punctuation, and no table in a reply |\n48: | End a turn · report work done, blocked, or partly done · end a turn while something you started is still running · ask the operator anything · end a turn on a fork or two acceptable paths · continue past a decision nobody made | [`communication-handoff.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md) | What is the operator's to do next, what is still running and what resumes it, and when a question becomes a structured choice |\n49: | Wire, rewire or remove a mode in a parent-hub skill · edit a hub's registry, router, root `ROUTER.md`, `graph-metadata.json` or `SKILL.md` mode table, or a mode packet's own `ROUTER.md` · report that a mode is registered, routed, reachable or integrated · quote a per-hub gate result · create a new skill under a hub, or refactor one that already lives there | [`skill-hub-routing.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/skill-hub-routing.md) | The two routing stages, what \"integrated\" requires, and checking the hub you actually changed |\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 3. INDEX\n54: \n55: | Rule | Summary |\n56: |------|---------|\n57: | [Overengineering](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md) | Build the smallest thing that solves the stated problem; take a costlier move only by naming what fails at the cheaper one. |\n58: | [Scope discipline](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md) | The requested scope is the deliverable. Adjacent problems get named, not fixed. |\n59: | [Evidence and proof](.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md) | A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it, and a receipt confirms only what could have contradicted it. Distinguish observed from derived from inferred. |\n60: | [Delegation and orchestration](.skilled/repo-rules/delegation-and-orchestration.md) | Delegating makes you the orchestrator; brief with evidence, and no single model's verdict closes a question. |\n61: | [Blast radius](.skilled/repo-rules/blast-radius.md) | Size effort to what the change can break; no irreversible step without a named rollback and a yes. |\n62: | [Root cause](.skilled/repo-rules/root-cause-and-debugging.md) | Fix the producer, not the symptom; every fix names the mechanism that caused the failure. |\n63: | [Uncertainty and honesty](.skilled/repo-rules/uncertainty-and-honesty.md) | Never fabricate; mark the confidence you actually have and halt on a contradiction. |\n64: | [Communication](.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md) | Write so the reader can act after one pass: no table in a reply, nothing that does not carry information. |\n65: | [Communication handoff](.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md) | End every turn by naming what is now the operator's to do, in the form that lets them do it. |\n66: | [Hub routing](.skilled/repo-rules/skill-hub-routing.md) | A hub routes in two stages, so a mode registered on one surface is not reachable, and a gate run without its hub argument reports on a hub you did not touch. |\n67: \n68: Each file expands `AGENTS.md` and is bounded by it: where a rule file appears to\n69: permit something `AGENTS.md` restricts, `AGENTS.md` wins and the rule file is wrong.\n70: \n71: ---\n72: \n73: ## 4. SCOPE OF THIS DOCUMENT\n74: \n75: **In:** how to think and act, restraint, scope, evidence, risk, diagnosis, honesty,\n76: the posture to hold when work is handed to another runtime, how the resulting reply\n77: reads, what you may claim about wiring you have changed, and how a turn hands control\n78: back to the operator. The delegation posture was the first widening and Delivery the\n79: second, added when `AGENTS.md` §8 moved down. Delivery is one of two rules here whose\n80: trigger is a whole turn rather than a specific action, the other being the handback rule,\n81: which fires at every turn's end, and `AGENTS.md` §4, under Reply Rules and Mandates, keeps\n82: the two clauses that must bind even when nothing loads.\n83: \n84: **Out:** skill routing, workflow selection, spec-folder mechanics, and the *mechanics*\n85: of agent and CLI dispatch: which agent, which command, which model, which flags.\n86: Those belong to `AGENTS.md` §2 and the skills it routes to, and are deliberately\n87: absent here so each has exactly one place to change. The line is between plumbing and\n88: posture: how to dispatch is theirs, how to think while dispatching is ours.\n89: \n90: **The routing carve-out, added deliberately as the third widening.** *Selecting* a\n91: route stays Out. *Verifying wiring you changed, and what you may claim about it*, is\n92: In; it is an evidence obligation whose subject happens to be routing. `skill-hub-routing.md`\n93: is the one rule on this side of that line, and it carries no route-selection guidance:\n94: the mechanics stay in the skills, and the rule points at them. A fourth widening that\n95: admits selection itself would dissolve the boundary; this one does not.\n96: \n97: **The ask-surface carve-out, added as the fourth widening, on an operator decision that\n98: overrode a research refusal.** A four-iteration decision-test run returned *refuse* here:\n99: naming a question tool per runtime reads as the \"which command\" family, and the paragraph\n100: above pre-refuses a fourth widening that admits selection. The operator widened it anyway,\n101: and what follows is the narrowing that keeps the boundary standing. *Choosing between\n102: runtimes, agents, commands, models or flags* stays Out, unchanged. *Naming the surface that\n103: asks the operator a question, in the runtime you are already running in*, is In. That is not\n104: a selection, because nothing is being selected: the runtime is a given, and the rule records\n105: which of its surfaces carries an obligation the rule already imposes. `communication-handoff.md`\n106: is the one rule on this side of that line, its §5 is the only place a tool name appears, and\n107: it names only what this repository confirms. A fifth widening that let a rule pick between\n108: runtimes would be the dissolution this one avoids.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/REPO RULES.md, lines 1-108\n1: # REPO RULES\n2: \n3: Repo-local operating rules. `AGENTS.md` **Gate 5 (§2)** makes reading this mandatory\n4: before your first write of the session; this document then routes you to every rule\n5: file that governs what you are about to do. **It is a router, not a rulebook:** it\n6: holds no rules of its own.\n7: \n8: ---\n9: \n10: ## 1. HOW TO USE THIS\n11: \n12: 1. **Match on the action you are about to take**, not the topic of the request.\n13: 2. **Load before the action.** A rule read afterwards is a post-mortem.\n14: 3. **A file already in context is not re-read.**\n15: 4. **Every trigger that fires is loaded, not just the first.** They compose; the more\n16:    specific wins on conflict. Three and four firing at once is the normal case, not an\n17:    edge case.\n18: 5. **Nothing fires → `AGENTS.md` alone governs.** Do not hunt for a rule to apply.\n19: \n20: ### Precedence\n21: \n22: | Level | Source | Can be overridden? |\n23: |-------|--------|--------------------|\n24: | 1 | Every `AGENTS.md` §1 hard blocker, the Four Laws, PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK, Comment Hygiene, and every mandatory gate in §2 | No |\n25: | 2 | An explicit, in-the-moment operator instruction | Not applicable, it is the instruction |\n26: | 3 | These rule files, and the guidance in a skill's `SKILL.md` | Only by level 1 or 2 |\n27: | 4 | General judgment | By anything above |\n28: \n29: A rule file may tighten `AGENTS.md`. None relaxes a HARD BLOCK or authorizes what\n30: `AGENTS.md` forbids. Gate 5 does not change that: it makes the **load** mandatory,\n31: while what you load stays at level 3, the obligation to read is tier 1, the content\n32: is not.\n33: \n34: ---\n35: \n36: ## 2. TRIGGER TABLE\n37: \n38: | You are about to… | Load | It settles |\n39: |-------------------|------|-----------|\n40: | Add a file, module, class, interface, option, layer, or dependency · write a spec or plan that adds one · generalize something that works · write \"flexible\", \"future-proof\", \"scalable\", \"extensible\", \"might need\", \"best practice\", \"while we're here\" · add a test beyond the coverage floor | [`prevent-overengineering.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md) | Whether this should exist at all, and at what size |\n41: | Touch a file outside the ask · fix something noticed in passing · change something else because it would make the fix easier · rename, reformat, or delete beyond the named area · deviate from an approved plan · decide what to do with the rest when part of the work is blocked · notice a defect, smell or stale comment outside the files in scope | [`scope-discipline.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md) | What is yours to change, and how to raise what isn't |\n42: | Say \"done\", \"works\", \"fixed\", \"passing\", \"no regressions\" · report a result · quote a number · act on a tool's or sub-agent's success report · close out a turn · report a file path or command output · write a completion summary or tick something off as done | [`evidence-and-proof.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md) | What counts as proof, how a green run lies, what an honest close-out contains |\n43: | Decide whether to hand work to another runtime at all · hand it to a CLI executor, sub-agent, fan-out lineage, or deep loop · compose the prompt one will act on · accept or quote what one returned · answer a judgment question from your own reading alone | [`delegation-and-orchestration.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/delegation-and-orchestration.md) | The orchestrating posture, what a brief must carry, why one model is one opinion |\n44: | Delete, overwrite, migrate, deploy, publish, send, install · force-push or rewrite history · change a shared contract · touch auth, data, or config · make any call that leaves this machine · truncate · touch branches, tags, or reflogs | [`blast-radius.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/blast-radius.md) | Reversibility, the rollback sentence, when to stop for a yes |\n45: | Diagnose a failure · make a red check green · attempt the same fix twice · add a special case, retry, sleep, or broadened catch · call a failure a flake, infra, or pre-existing | [`root-cause-and-debugging.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/root-cause-and-debugging.md) | Fixing the producer instead of the symptom, and when to level up to the seam |\n46: | Answer without certainty · contradict the operator · fill a gap with a plausible guess · hit a contradiction between two things that must both be true · name a path, flag, function, version, or number you have not verified · not know while a plausible answer is available · see sources disagree, or the code contradict the spec, the docs or the operator · the operator asserts something you believe is wrong · change a checked answer after pushback or doubt, or drop an approach before it concludes · cite a rule, restriction, policy, limit or permission, or decline a request | [`uncertainty-and-honesty.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/uncertainty-and-honesty.md) | Confidence bands, UNKNOWN, contradiction halts |\n47: | Write any substantive reply, an answer, an explanation, a close-out or a status · draft or edit any sentence a reader will read · present a recommendation, a fork, or a trade-off · start a multi-step stretch of work the reader will not see inside · report what a long autonomous run found · the reader says they did not follow or asks for a plainer version | [`communication.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md) | How a reply reads: answer first, one recommended path, length, filler, plain sentences, punctuation, and no table in a reply |\n48: | End a turn · report work done, blocked, or partly done · end a turn while something you started is still running · ask the operator anything · end a turn on a fork or two acceptable paths · continue past a decision nobody made | [`communication-handoff.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md) | What is the operator's to do next, what is still running and what resumes it, and when a question becomes a structured choice |\n49: | Wire, rewire or remove a mode in a parent-hub skill · edit a hub's registry, router, root `ROUTER.md`, `graph-metadata.json` or `SKILL.md` mode table, or a mode packet's own `ROUTER.md` · report that a mode is registered, routed, reachable or integrated · quote a per-hub gate result · create a new skill under a hub, or refactor one that already lives there | [`skill-hub-routing.md`](.skilled/repo-rules/skill-hub-routing.md) | The two routing stages, what \"integrated\" requires, and checking the hub you actually changed |\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 3. INDEX\n54: \n55: | Rule | Summary |\n56: |------|---------|\n57: | [Overengineering](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md) | Build the smallest thing that solves the stated problem; take a costlier move only by naming what fails at the cheaper one. |\n58: | [Scope discipline](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md) | The requested scope is the deliverable. Adjacent problems get named, not fixed. |\n59: | [Evidence and proof](.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md) | A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it, and a receipt confirms only what could have contradicted it. Distinguish observed from derived from inferred. |\n60: | [Delegation and orchestration](.skilled/repo-rules/delegation-and-orchestration.md) | Delegating makes you the orchestrator; brief with evidence, and no single model's verdict closes a question. |\n61: | [Blast radius](.skilled/repo-rules/blast-radius.md) | Size effort to what the change can break; no irreversible step without a named rollback and a yes. |\n62: | [Root cause](.skilled/repo-rules/root-cause-and-debugging.md) | Fix the producer, not the symptom; every fix names the mechanism that caused the failure. |\n63: | [Uncertainty and honesty](.skilled/repo-rules/uncertainty-and-honesty.md) | Never fabricate; mark the confidence you actually have and halt on a contradiction. |\n64: | [Communication](.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md) | Write so the reader can act after one pass: no table in a reply, nothing that does not carry information. |\n65: | [Communication handoff](.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md) | End every turn by naming what is now the operator's to do, in the form that lets them do it. |\n66: | [Hub routing](.skilled/repo-rules/skill-hub-routing.md) | A hub routes in two stages, so a mode registered on one surface is not reachable, and a gate run without its hub argument reports on a hub you did not touch. |\n67: \n68: Each file expands `AGENTS.md` and is bounded by it: where a rule file appears to\n69: permit something `AGENTS.md` restricts, `AGENTS.md` wins and the rule file is wrong.\n70: \n71: ---\n72: \n73: ## 4. SCOPE OF THIS DOCUMENT\n74: \n75: **In:** how to think and act, restraint, scope, evidence, risk, diagnosis, honesty,\n76: the posture to hold when work is handed to another runtime, how the resulting reply\n77: reads, what you may claim about wiring you have changed, and how a turn hands control\n78: back to the operator. The delegation posture was the first widening and Delivery the\n79: second, added when `AGENTS.md` §8 moved down. Delivery is one of two rules here whose\n80: trigger is a whole turn rather than a specific action, the other being the handback rule,\n81: which fires at every turn's end, and `AGENTS.md` §4, under Reply Rules and Mandates, keeps\n82: the two clauses that must bind even when nothing loads.\n83: \n84: **Out:** skill routing, workflow selection, spec-folder mechanics, and the *mechanics*\n85: of agent and CLI dispatch: which agent, which command, which model, which flags.\n86: Those belong to `AGENTS.md` §2 and the skills it routes to, and are deliberately\n87: absent here so each has exactly one place to change. The line is between plumbing and\n88: posture: how to dispatch is theirs, how to think while dispatching is ours.\n89: \n90: **The routing carve-out, added deliberately as the third widening.** *Selecting* a\n91: route stays Out. *Verifying wiring you changed, and what you may claim about it*, is\n92: In; it is an evidence obligation whose subject happens to be routing. `skill-hub-routing.md`\n93: is the one rule on this side of that line, and it carries no route-selection guidance:\n94: the mechanics stay in the skills, and the rule points at them. A fourth widening that\n95: admits selection itself would dissolve the boundary; this one does not.\n96: \n97: **The ask-surface carve-out, added as the fourth widening, on an operator decision that\n98: overrode a research refusal.** A four-iteration decision-test run returned *refuse* here:\n99: naming a question tool per runtime reads as the \"which command\" family, and the paragraph\n100: above pre-refuses a fourth widening that admits selection. The operator widened it anyway,\n101: and what follows is the narrowing that keeps the boundary standing. *Choosing between\n102: runtimes, agents, commands, models or flags* stays Out, unchanged. *Naming the surface that\n103: asks the operator a question, in the runtime you are already running in*, is In. That is not\n104: a selection, because nothing is being selected: the runtime is a given, and the rule records\n105: which of its surfaces carries an obligation the rule already imposes. `communication-handoff.md`\n106: is the one rule on this side of that line, its §5 is the only place a tool name appears, and\n107: it names only what this repository confirms. A fifth widening that let a rule pick between\n108: runtimes would be the dissolution this one avoids."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/REPO RULES.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794539498452,"end":1794539499176}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794539499183,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1dfed7ffelzC6M9OLNWqvFE","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2e3acde001UosaR7wZ6551Fm","sessionID":"ses_e2d1dfed7ffelzC6M9OLNWqvFE","messageID":"msg_1d2e39df4001g1AvmGSj5ZN5rk","type":"tool","id":"call_230407d0e98b49a8ab8f2b1e","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs, lines 1-248\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: EMBEDDER COST MEASUREMENT\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: //\n5: // Records what the local embedder costs so a reader can reproduce the numbers\n6: // the install guides quote. The server probes read the Ollama version, the\n7: // model's size on disk, the loaded size and expiry and the resident memory of\n8: // `ollama serve` and its model runner. The embedding section then times the\n9: // query embedding the scoring path sends, 30 times, through the shared\n10: // adapter, and keeps the first call apart so a cold start has its own number.\n11: // A final section times five end-to-end `advisor_recommend` calls, so the same\n12: // run also reports the wait a prompt hook pays for a route.\n13: // The run writes, starts and unloads nothing: a cold sample loads the model as\n14: // any first query would, and Ollama's own idle timer unloads it later.\n15: //\n16: // Usage:\n17: //   node measure-embedder-cost.mjs    # print one JSON object to stdout\n18: //\n19: // A server that does not answer leaves every number unreachable, so the run\n20: // stops there with exit 2 and names the URL it tried.\n21: \n22: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: // 1. IMPORTS\n24: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n25: \n26: import { execFileSync, spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\n27: import { dirname, resolve } from 'node:path';\n28: import { fileURLToPath, pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\n29: import { OllamaAdapter } from '../../../system-spec-kit/shared/dist/embeddings/adapters/ollama.js';\n30: import { getManifest } from '../../../system-spec-kit/shared/dist/embeddings/registry.js';\n31: \n32: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n33: // 2. CONSTANTS\n34: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n35: \n36: const MODEL_NAME = 'nomic-embed-text:v1.5';\n37: const MODEL_MANIFEST = 'nomic-embed-text-v1.5';\n38: const DEFAULT_BASE_URL = 'http://127.0.0.1:11434';\n39: const PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS = 5000;\n40: const WARM_SAMPLE_COUNT = 30;\n41: const SCRIPT_DIR = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\n42: const REPO_ROOT = resolve(SCRIPT_DIR, '../../../../..');\n43: const CLI_PATH = resolve(REPO_ROOT, '.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs');\n44: const CLI_TIMEOUT_MS = 120000;\n45: const CLI_PROMPTS = [\n46:   'review this pull request for type safety',\n47:   'debug the failing scorer test',\n48:   'write a guide for the install step',\n49:   'design a chart for the cost table',\n50:   'plan the release checklist order',\n51: ];\n52: \n53: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n54: // 3. SERVER PROBES\n55: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n56: \n57: function ollamaBaseUrl() {\n58:   const configured = process.env.OLLAMA_BASE_URL?.trim();\n59:   return (configured && configured.length > 0 ? configured : DEFAULT_BASE_URL).replace(/\\/+$/, '');\n60: }\n61: \n62: async function getJson(url) {\n63:   const response = await fetch(url, { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS) });\n64:   if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`GET ${url} returned HTTP ${response.status}`);\n65:   return response.json();\n66: }\n67: \n68: // The size on disk belongs to the pulled model, not to the loaded copy, so it\n69: // comes from `/api/tags`. A missing tag makes the measurement impossible and is\n70: // reported rather than printed as a null a reader could mistake for zero.\n71: function modelFromTags(tags) {\n72:   const listed = Array.isArray(tags?.models) ? tags.models : [];\n73:   const model = listed.find((entry) => entry?.name === MODEL_NAME);\n74:   if (!model) throw new Error(`${MODEL_NAME} is not in GET /api/tags`);\n75:   return { name: model.name, sizeBytes: model.size ?? null };\n76: }\n77: \n78: // `/api/ps` lists one entry per loaded model and keeps the loaded copy's size\n79: // apart from the size on disk. No matching entry means the model is unloaded,\n80: // which is a state the cost reader has to see rather than an error.\n81: function loadedFromPs(ps) {\n82:   const listed = Array.isArray(ps?.models) ? ps.models : [];\n83:   const model = listed.find((entry) => entry?.name === MODEL_NAME);\n84:   if (!model) return null;\n85:   return {\n86:     name: model.name,\n87:     sizeBytes: model.size ?? null,\n88:     sizeVramBytes: model.size_vram ?? null,\n89:     expiresAt: model.expires_at ?? null,\n90:   };\n91: }\n92: \n93: // `ps -axo` prints one row per process, with the command last so it may hold\n94: // spaces. A wrapper shell that mentions `ollama serve` in its own command line\n95: // is excluded by requiring the executable at the start of the row to be ollama,\n96: // not merely by finding that text later in it.\n97: function processRows() {\n98:   const output = execFileSync('ps', ['-axo', 'pid,rss,command'], { encoding: 'utf8' });\n99:   const rows = [];\n100:   for (const line of output.split('\\n')) {\n101:     const match = /^\\s*(\\d+)\\s+(\\d+)\\s+(.*)$/.exec(line);\n102:     if (match === null) continue;\n103:     rows.push({ pid: Number(match[1]), rssKb: Number(match[2]), command: match[3] });\n104:   }\n105:   return rows;\n106: }\n107: \n108: function memoryFromProcesses(rows) {\n109:   const serve = rows.find((row) => /^\\S*ollama\\s+serve(?:\\s|$)/.test(row.command));\n110:   const runner = rows.find((row) => /(?:^|\\/)llama-server(?:\\s|$)/.test(row.command) || /\\bollama\\s+runner(?:\\s|$)/.test(row.command));\n111:   return {\n112:     servePid: serve?.pid ?? null,\n113:     serveRssKb: serve?.rssKb ?? null,\n114:     runnerPid: runner?.pid ?? null,\n115:     runnerRssKb: runner?.rssKb ?? null,\n116:   };\n117: }\n118: \n119: async function measureServer() {\n120:   const baseUrl = ollamaBaseUrl();\n121:   let version;\n122:   try {\n123:     const payload = await getJson(`${baseUrl}/api/version`);\n124:     version = typeof payload?.version === 'string' ? payload.version : null;\n125:   } catch {\n126:     process.stderr.write(`ollama server not answering at ${baseUrl}\\n`);\n127:     process.exit(2);\n128:   }\n129: \n130:   const [tags, ps] = await Promise.all([getJson(`${baseUrl}/api/tags`), getJson(`${baseUrl}/api/ps`)]);\n131:   return {\n132:     server: { url: baseUrl, version },\n133:     model: modelFromTags(tags),\n134:     loaded: loadedFromPs(ps),\n135:     memory: memoryFromProcesses(processRows()),\n136:   };\n137: }\n138: \n139: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n140: // 4. EMBEDDING MEASUREMENT\n141: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n142: \n143: // Percentiles use the nearest-rank definition the runtime metrics report with,\n144: // so a p95 here and a p95 in a routing capture count the same way.\n145: function percentile(values, fraction) {\n146:   const sorted = [...values].sort((a, b) => a - b);\n147:   const rank = Math.min(sorted.length - 1, Math.ceil(fraction * sorted.length) - 1);\n148:   return sorted[rank];\n149: }\n150: \n151: function roundMs(value) {\n152:   return Number(value.toFixed(2));\n153: }\n154: \n155: function summariseSamples(samples) {\n156:   return {\n157:     n: samples.length,\n158:     medianMs: roundMs(percentile(samples, 0.5)),\n159:     p95Ms: roundMs(percentile(samples, 0.95)),\n160:   };\n161: }\n162: \n163: async function embedOnce(adapter, text) {\n164:   const started = performance.now();\n165:   await adapter.embed([text], { inputType: 'query' });\n166:   return performance.now() - started;\n167: }\n168: \n169: // The first call is measured on its own. When the model was unloaded it pays the\n170: // load and is the cold number, and when it was already loaded it is a discarded\n171: // warm-up, so the 30 timed calls that follow are warm samples in either state.\n172: // Distinct texts keep a repeated query from measuring a repeat-hit shortcut\n173: // instead of the embedding path a real prompt takes.\n174: async function measureEmbeddings(baseUrl, startedCold) {\n175:   const manifest = getManifest(MODEL_MANIFEST);\n176:   if (manifest === undefined) throw new Error(`embedder manifest ${MODEL_MANIFEST} is not registered`);\n177:   const adapter = new OllamaAdapter(manifest, { baseUrl });\n178: \n179:   const firstCallMs = roundMs(await embedOnce(adapter, 'measure the embedder cost 0'));\n180:   const samples = [];\n181:   for (let index = 1; index <= WARM_SAMPLE_COUNT; index += 1) {\n182:     samples.push(await embedOnce(adapter, `measure the embedder cost ${index}`));\n183:   }\n184: \n185:   return {\n186:     warm: summariseSamples(samples),\n187:     cold: startedCold ? { firstCallMs } : null,\n188:     coldReason: startedCold ? null : 'model already loaded',\n189:   };\n190: }\n191: \n192: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n193: // 5. CLI MEASUREMENT\n194: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n195: \n196: // Each call spawns the CLI the prompt hook spawns, so the number includes the\n197: // process start, the daemon round trip and the scoring, which is the wait a user\n198: // of the hook pays. Distinct prompts keep a repeat-hit shortcut out of the\n199: // timing and cover more of the scorer than one sentence would.\n200: function measureCliOnce(prompt) {\n201:   const started = performance.now();\n202:   const result = spawnSync(\n203:     process.execPath,\n204:     [CLI_PATH, 'advisor_recommend', '--json', JSON.stringify({ prompt }), '--format', 'json'],\n205:     { cwd: REPO_ROOT, encoding: 'utf8', timeout: CLI_TIMEOUT_MS },\n206:   );\n207:   const elapsedMs = performance.now() - started;\n208:   if (result.error) throw new Error(`advisor_recommend failed: ${result.error.message}`);\n209:   if (result.status !== 0) {\n210:     const detail = (result.stderr ?? '').trim().split('\\n')[0];\n211:     throw new Error(`advisor_recommend exited ${result.status}${detail.length > 0 ? `: ${detail}` : ''}`);\n212:   }\n213:   return elapsedMs;\n214: }\n215: \n216: function measureCli() {\n217:   const samples = CLI_PROMPTS.map((prompt) => roundMs(measureCliOnce(prompt)));\n218:   return { ms: samples, medianMs: roundMs(percentile(samples, 0.5)) };\n219: }\n220: \n221: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n222: // 6. CLI ENTRY\n223: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n224: \n225: if (process.argv[1] && import.meta.url === pathToFileURL(resolve(process.argv[1])).href) {\n226:   try {\n227:     const measured = await measureServer();\n228:     // An unloaded model is the only state in which the next embed pays the load,\n229:     // so it is also the only state where the serve memory is still idle.\n230:     const startedCold = measured.loaded === null;\n231:     const embeddings = await measureEmbeddings(measured.server.url, startedCold);\n232:     const cost = {\n233:       server: measured.server,\n234:       model: measured.model,\n235:       loaded: measured.loaded,\n236:       memory: measured.memory,\n237:       idle: startedCold ? { serveRssKb: measured.memory.serveRssKb } : null,\n238:       warm: embeddings.warm,\n239:       cold: embeddings.cold,\n240:       coldReason: embeddings.coldReason,\n241:       cli: measureCli(),\n242:     };\n243:     console.log(JSON.stringify(cost, null, 2));\n244:   } catch (error) {\n245:     process.stderr.write(`measure-embedder-cost.mjs: ${error.message}\\n`);\n246:     process.exit(2);\n247:   }\n248: }","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs, lines 1-248\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: EMBEDDER COST MEASUREMENT\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: //\n5: // Records what the local embedder costs so a reader can reproduce the numbers\n6: // the install guides quote. The server probes read the Ollama version, the\n7: // model's size on disk, the loaded size and expiry and the resident memory of\n8: // `ollama serve` and its model runner. The embedding section then times the\n9: // query embedding the scoring path sends, 30 times, through the shared\n10: // adapter, and keeps the first call apart so a cold start has its own number.\n11: // A final section times five end-to-end `advisor_recommend` calls, so the same\n12: // run also reports the wait a prompt hook pays for a route.\n13: // The run writes, starts and unloads nothing: a cold sample loads the model as\n14: // any first query would, and Ollama's own idle timer unloads it later.\n15: //\n16: // Usage:\n17: //   node measure-embedder-cost.mjs    # print one JSON object to stdout\n18: //\n19: // A server that does not answer leaves every number unreachable, so the run\n20: // stops there with exit 2 and names the URL it tried.\n21: \n22: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: // 1. IMPORTS\n24: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n25: \n26: import { execFileSync, spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\n27: import { dirname, resolve } from 'node:path';\n28: import { fileURLToPath, pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\n29: import { OllamaAdapter } from '../../../system-spec-kit/shared/dist/embeddings/adapters/ollama.js';\n30: import { getManifest } from '../../../system-spec-kit/shared/dist/embeddings/registry.js';\n31: \n32: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n33: // 2. CONSTANTS\n34: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n35: \n36: const MODEL_NAME = 'nomic-embed-text:v1.5';\n37: const MODEL_MANIFEST = 'nomic-embed-text-v1.5';\n38: const DEFAULT_BASE_URL = 'http://127.0.0.1:11434';\n39: const PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS = 5000;\n40: const WARM_SAMPLE_COUNT = 30;\n41: const SCRIPT_DIR = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\n42: const REPO_ROOT = resolve(SCRIPT_DIR, '../../../../..');\n43: const CLI_PATH = resolve(REPO_ROOT, '.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs');\n44: const CLI_TIMEOUT_MS = 120000;\n45: const CLI_PROMPTS = [\n46:   'review this pull request for type safety',\n47:   'debug the failing scorer test',\n48:   'write a guide for the install step',\n49:   'design a chart for the cost table',\n50:   'plan the release checklist order',\n51: ];\n52: \n53: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n54: // 3. SERVER PROBES\n55: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n56: \n57: function ollamaBaseUrl() {\n58:   const configured = process.env.OLLAMA_BASE_URL?.trim();\n59:   return (configured && configured.length > 0 ? configured : DEFAULT_BASE_URL).replace(/\\/+$/, '');\n60: }\n61: \n62: async function getJson(url) {\n63:   const response = await fetch(url, { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS) });\n64:   if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`GET ${url} returned HTTP ${response.status}`);\n65:   return response.json();\n66: }\n67: \n68: // The size on disk belongs to the pulled model, not to the loaded copy, so it\n69: // comes from `/api/tags`. A missing tag makes the measurement impossible and is\n70: // reported rather than printed as a null a reader could mistake for zero.\n71: function modelFromTags(tags) {\n72:   const listed = Array.isArray(tags?.models) ? tags.models : [];\n73:   const model = listed.find((entry) => entry?.name === MODEL_NAME);\n74:   if (!model) throw new Error(`${MODEL_NAME} is not in GET /api/tags`);\n75:   return { name: model.name, sizeBytes: model.size ?? null };\n76: }\n77: \n78: // `/api/ps` lists one entry per loaded model and keeps the loaded copy's size\n79: // apart from the size on disk. No matching entry means the model is unloaded,\n80: // which is a state the cost reader has to see rather than an error.\n81: function loadedFromPs(ps) {\n82:   const listed = Array.isArray(ps?.models) ? ps.models : [];\n83:   const model = listed.find((entry) => entry?.name === MODEL_NAME);\n84:   if (!model) return null;\n85:   return {\n86:     name: model.name,\n87:     sizeBytes: model.size ?? null,\n88:     sizeVramBytes: model.size_vram ?? null,\n89:     expiresAt: model.expires_at ?? null,\n90:   };\n91: }\n92: \n93: // `ps -axo` prints one row per process, with the command last so it may hold\n94: // spaces. A wrapper shell that mentions `ollama serve` in its own command line\n95: // is excluded by requiring the executable at the start of the row to be ollama,\n96: // not merely by finding that text later in it.\n97: function processRows() {\n98:   const output = execFileSync('ps', ['-axo', 'pid,rss,command'], { encoding: 'utf8' });\n99:   const rows = [];\n100:   for (const line of output.split('\\n')) {\n101:     const match = /^\\s*(\\d+)\\s+(\\d+)\\s+(.*)$/.exec(line);\n102:     if (match === null) continue;\n103:     rows.push({ pid: Number(match[1]), rssKb: Number(match[2]), command: match[3] });\n104:   }\n105:   return rows;\n106: }\n107: \n108: function memoryFromProcesses(rows) {\n109:   const serve = rows.find((row) => /^\\S*ollama\\s+serve(?:\\s|$)/.test(row.command));\n110:   const runner = rows.find((row) => /(?:^|\\/)llama-server(?:\\s|$)/.test(row.command) || /\\bollama\\s+runner(?:\\s|$)/.test(row.command));\n111:   return {\n112:     servePid: serve?.pid ?? null,\n113:     serveRssKb: serve?.rssKb ?? null,\n114:     runnerPid: runner?.pid ?? null,\n115:     runnerRssKb: runner?.rssKb ?? null,\n116:   };\n117: }\n118: \n119: async function measureServer() {\n120:   const baseUrl = ollamaBaseUrl();\n121:   let version;\n122:   try {\n123:     const payload = await getJson(`${baseUrl}/api/version`);\n124:     version = typeof payload?.version === 'string' ? payload.version : null;\n125:   } catch {\n126:     process.stderr.write(`ollama server not answering at ${baseUrl}\\n`);\n127:     process.exit(2);\n128:   }\n129: \n130:   const [tags, ps] = await Promise.all([getJson(`${baseUrl}/api/tags`), getJson(`${baseUrl}/api/ps`)]);\n131:   return {\n132:     server: { url: baseUrl, version },\n133:     model: modelFromTags(tags),\n134:     loaded: loadedFromPs(ps),\n135:     memory: memoryFromProcesses(processRows()),\n136:   };\n137: }\n138: \n139: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n140: // 4. EMBEDDING MEASUREMENT\n141: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n142: \n143: // Percentiles use the nearest-rank definition the runtime metrics report with,\n144: // so a p95 here and a p95 in a routing capture count the same way.\n145: function percentile(values, fraction) {\n146:   const sorted = [...values].sort((a, b) => a - b);\n147:   const rank = Math.min(sorted.length - 1, Math.ceil(fraction * sorted.length) - 1);\n148:   return sorted[rank];\n149: }\n150: \n151: function roundMs(value) {\n152:   return Number(value.toFixed(2));\n153: }\n154: \n155: function summariseSamples(samples) {\n156:   return {\n157:     n: samples.length,\n158:     medianMs: roundMs(percentile(samples, 0.5)),\n159:     p95Ms: roundMs(percentile(samples, 0.95)),\n160:   };\n161: }\n162: \n163: async function embedOnce(adapter, text) {\n164:   const started = performance.now();\n165:   await adapter.embed([text], { inputType: 'query' });\n166:   return performance.now() - started;\n167: }\n168: \n169: // The first call is measured on its own. When the model was unloaded it pays the\n170: // load and is the cold number, and when it was already loaded it is a discarded\n171: // warm-up, so the 30 timed calls that follow are warm samples in either state.\n172: // Distinct texts keep a repeated query from measuring a repeat-hit shortcut\n173: // instead of the embedding path a real prompt takes.\n174: async function measureEmbeddings(baseUrl, startedCold) {\n175:   const manifest = getManifest(MODEL_MANIFEST);\n176:   if (manifest === undefined) throw new Error(`embedder manifest ${MODEL_MANIFEST} is not registered`);\n177:   const adapter = new OllamaAdapter(manifest, { baseUrl });\n178: \n179:   const firstCallMs = roundMs(await embedOnce(adapter, 'measure the embedder cost 0'));\n180:   const samples = [];\n181:   for (let index = 1; index <= WARM_SAMPLE_COUNT; index += 1) {\n182:     samples.push(await embedOnce(adapter, `measure the embedder cost ${index}`));\n183:   }\n184: \n185:   return {\n186:     warm: summariseSamples(samples),\n187:     cold: startedCold ? { firstCallMs } : null,\n188:     coldReason: startedCold ? null : 'model already loaded',\n189:   };\n190: }\n191: \n192: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n193: // 5. CLI MEASUREMENT\n194: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n195: \n196: // Each call spawns the CLI the prompt hook spawns, so the number includes the\n197: // process start, the daemon round trip and the scoring, which is the wait a user\n198: // of the hook pays. Distinct prompts keep a repeat-hit shortcut out of the\n199: // timing and cover more of the scorer than one sentence would.\n200: function measureCliOnce(prompt) {\n201:   const started = performance.now();\n202:   const result = spawnSync(\n203:     process.execPath,\n204:     [CLI_PATH, 'advisor_recommend', '--json', JSON.stringify({ prompt }), '--format', 'json'],\n205:     { cwd: REPO_ROOT, encoding: 'utf8', timeout: CLI_TIMEOUT_MS },\n206:   );\n207:   const elapsedMs = performance.now() - started;\n208:   if (result.error) throw new Error(`advisor_recommend failed: ${result.error.message}`);\n209:   if (result.status !== 0) {\n210:     const detail = (result.stderr ?? '').trim().split('\\n')[0];\n211:     throw new Error(`advisor_recommend exited ${result.status}${detail.length > 0 ? `: ${detail}` : ''}`);\n212:   }\n213:   return elapsedMs;\n214: }\n215: \n216: function measureCli() {\n217:   const samples = CLI_PROMPTS.map((prompt) => roundMs(measureCliOnce(prompt)));\n218:   return { ms: samples, medianMs: roundMs(percentile(samples, 0.5)) };\n219: }\n220: \n221: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n222: // 6. CLI ENTRY\n223: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n224: \n225: if (process.argv[1] && import.meta.url === pathToFileURL(resolve(process.argv[1])).href) {\n226:   try {\n227:     const measured = await measureServer();\n228:     // An unloaded model is the only state in which the next embed pays the load,\n229:     // so it is also the only state where the serve memory is still idle.\n230:     const startedCold = measured.loaded === null;\n231:     const embeddings = await measureEmbeddings(measured.server.url, startedCold);\n232:     const cost = {\n233:       server: measured.server,\n234:       model: measured.model,\n235:       loaded: measured.loaded,\n236:       memory: measured.memory,\n237:       idle: startedCold ? { serveRssKb: measured.memory.serveRssKb } : null,\n238:       warm: embeddings.warm,\n239:       cold: embeddings.cold,\n240:       coldReason: embeddings.coldReason,\n241:       cli: measureCli(),\n242:     };\n243:     console.log(JSON.stringify(cost, null, 2));\n244:   } catch (error) {\n245:     process.stderr.write(`measure-embedder-cost.mjs: ${error.message}\\n`);\n246:     process.exit(2);\n247:   }\n248: }"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794539498718,"end":1794539499183}}}}
