{"type":"text","timestamp":1794540000823,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1dfed7ffelzC6M9OLNWqvFE","part":{"id":"prt_1d2eb46d8001kLpFgNtesBq433","sessionID":"ses_e2d1dfed7ffelzC6M9OLNWqvFE","messageID":"msg_1d2eb27be0013OAvzaH3nxEZeU","type":"text","text":"T006 is implemented and verified.\n\n**File written**\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs` (new)\n\nIt reads the corpus under `--root`, keeps `typed`/`none` rows, refuses holdout and unknown ids before creating the sandbox, pipes the exact hook payload through the Claude prompt hook in a `ssa-cost-` temp socket directory with a 30s timeout, records UTF-8 bytes and `ceil(bytes / 4)` tokens, prints the summary object, then SIGTERMs only processes whose command line names that directory and removes it.\n\n**Verify output**\n\n```\n$ node --check .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs\ncheck exit=0\n\n$ node …/measure-brief-cost.mjs --rows cmd-speckit-save-typed-01 | jq -c '.rows[0] | [.id, (.bytes > 0), (.estimatedTokens == ((.bytes + 3) / 4 | floor))]'\n[\"cmd-speckit-save-typed-01\",true,true]\n\n$ node …/measure-brief-cost.mjs --rows \"$(jq -r 'select(.split==\"holdout\") | .id' $CORPUS | head -1)\"\n{\"error\":\"holdout_row\",\"id\":\"cmd-create-agent-plain-holdout-01\"}\nholdout exit=2\n\n$ ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-cost-* 2>/dev/null\nleftover exit=1        # no output, as required\n```\n\nA full 44-row run also succeeds: 44 rows, zero empty contexts, no leftover sandbox directory.\n\n**Note**\n\nThe current advisor dist is stale, so every hook call in this checkout resolves to the fail-open directive (`361`–`408` bytes) rather than a live brief. The task's verify only requires `bytes > 0`, so it passes, and wave 5 rebuilds before the real head measurements run. I did not rebuild, since that is outside T006's files.\n\n`tasks.md` was not ticked. No other file was modified by me.","time":{"start":1794539996888,"end":1794540000823}}}
